The instrumented run's "reserve dep=zn-r54 targets=0" was the CACHED index
answering. sessionWaitDependencyTargetsForDependency reads the index built from
observeSessionWaitCensus, which is a CACHE observation, so a wait registered
since that observation is invisible at the dependency's bead.closed - no
certificate is minted, no reservation is installed, and the poke's legacy tick
then advances the durable wait into legacy shape. The round-6 stand-down landed
at e4fcb01f5f had nothing to stand down for.

reserveSessionWaitDependencyTargets now falls back to resolving the closed
bead's WAITING DEPENDENTS from the durable wait rows. It is bounded, not a
fleet scan: one label-scoped gc:wait listing under the same
SessionWaitLookupLimit the cached census already pays, filtered to the exact
dependency before anything is certified, and skipped entirely whenever the
index can answer. A city with no pending waits at all collapses to one listing
per 250ms floor, because with none no bead.closed can ever name a dependent.

A durable-resolved target carries its own provenance
(sessionWaitDependencyDurableGeneration) instead of a published index
generation: the index cannot certify it - the index missing the wait is exactly
why the path exists - and certifySessionWaitDependencyStartLease already
re-reads BOTH durable rows before the lease is minted. The provenance survives
the backstop redrive, so a durable-resolved reservation is not downgraded on
its next pass. The patrol redrive is thereby demoted to the anti-entropy
backstop it should always have been; it is not deleted.

